# 0.5 (`REFUSED-DECLARATION-ID`): a `node` line refused for its ARITY
# declares nothing, like every other failing line (core §8.3.3 item 1, §8.3.4).
#
# Before this fix the engine recorded the node's id BEFORE its surplus-argument
# check, so a refused line still claimed the id. Two visible consequences, one
# section each.
#
# Section 1, the missing cascade: `node a "A" extra` is refused, so `edge a -> b`
# names an endpoint that was never declared and MUST be a second error,
# `unknown endpoint "a"`. The old engine reported only the first.
#
# Section 2, the false duplicate: the author repairs the line by writing it
# again. The corrected `node a "A"` is the FIRST declaration of `a`, so the
# section reports the refused line and nothing else. The old engine also
# answered `duplicate id "a"` on the repair.
#
# 920 pins the same cascade for a VALUE fault (`shape=hexagon`); this file pins
# it for an arity fault, which took a different code path.
figdown 0.5 block
node a "A" extra
node b "B"
edge a -> b

figdown 0.5 block
node a "A" extra
node a "A"
node b "B"
edge a -> b
